Since April, people have reported wrong dates in bookings, invites, and reminders. By 4 October,
the desk export held **412 unique reports** merged into #4471. The export has 427 rows because
15 reports appear again in overlapping pages; count each report ID once.

The reports describe **two separate problems**, not one large parser bug. The shared parser
accounts for **379 reports**. A second problem in the booking form's date hint accounts for
**33 reports**. File and track them separately so each fix can be verified against its own reports.

<Callout>
Known as one merged ticket; split into two actionable issues. The parser reads dates month-first
for day-first tenant locales. Separately, booking-v3 shows a month-first hint to day-first tenants;
people follow that hint and the form interprets their entry incorrectly.
</Callout>

## Diagnosis and issue split

| Problem | Reports | Tracking issue |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser ignores the tenant's day-first locale | 379 | [Issue #2](https://github.com/ngvhoang96/megadev-challenge-s01e03/issues/2) |
| booking-v3 date hint conflicts with a day-first tenant locale | 33 | [Issue #1](https://github.com/ngvhoang96/megadev-challenge-s01e03/issues/1) |

The desk's intake tag is only a guess. The split uses each report's tenant locale, form, and
channel, then deduplicates by report ID. Parser reports span 11 tenants; hint reports span 3.
Five reports noted as one-day moves remain filed under their actual cause; the symptom alone does
not define a third problem.

## Lessons

- A merged ticket can hide independent causes; classify by tenant, locale, form, and channel.
- Count unique report IDs, not export rows, when reports occur in overlapping pages.
- A familiar symptom is not enough to group reports; verify the cause before assigning a ticket.

